    "explanation": "The no-show fee stands, so the driver is owed the 5.00 SGD that was refunded to the rider on 24 Aug 2026 and withheld from him. Both accounts were read against the record.\n\nWhy the fee stands. Free wait (POL-NS-21): the driver arrived at 07:39:30 (auto-arrival, corroborated by the driver GPS trace — nearest fix 1.758 m from the pickup with 3 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and the 25 m filter; EV-TRIP-05058, EV-GPS-05058). The 300-second free wait ran to 07:44:30 and the driver cancelled at 07:51:40 — 430 seconds later (derived.v7.free_wait, EV-TRIP-05058). The rider's point that the driver came early is answered by the clause itself: the free wait runs from the driver's arrival, scheduled trip or not. Contact obligation (POL-NS-23): two in-app messages (07:40:00, read 07:40:22; 07:46:20, read 07:46:30) and two in-app calls (07:47:30, rang 28 s; 07:50:10, rang 20 s), all before the 07:51:40 cancellation (EV-CHAT-05058, in_app_calls in EV-TRIP-05058). Both limbs are met, so the fee is not voided — the rider's complaint that the messages and calls came only after the free wait expired does not matter, because the clause requires contact before cancelling, and that is what the record shows. Driver's own deadline (POL-NS-24): booked 07:45, deadline 07:50, and the driver arrived at 07:39:30 (arrived_by_deadline = true), so no FULL_REFUND arises; and because he did message and call, the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit attached to a no-contact no-show does not fire either. Fee (POL-NS-22): the fare breakdown charges 5.00 SGD and payment reconciles (fee_matches_policy = true, total_charged 5.00, EV-FARE-05058) — exactly the policy figure.\n\nWhy the case is not escalated. The driver's trace carries no rider track (rider_track is empty) and the third-party traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05058-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; I name both because the rider disclosed them. Neither is needed: no no-show rule